      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(cli): bind capability CLI media input reads to descriptor size",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `readCliInputFileSafely` function in `src/cli/capability-cli/media-output.ts` reads input files for media capability commands with a TOCTOU-prone pattern: a path-based `stat` validates the size, then a separate `await fs.readFile(path)` reads the content. Between the stat and the read, a file could be swapped with a much larger one, potentially causing OOM.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nMedia input files are user-supplied paths that could be symlink-swapped or grown between validation and consumption. Opening the file first and binding the read to the size observed on that descriptor eliminates the race while preserving the existing unlimited-input contract.\n\n## What Changed\n\nReplaced the path-based `stat` + `readFile` pattern with a descriptor-bound exact read:\n\n```typescript\nconst handle = await fs.open(resolvedPath, \\\"r\\\");\ntry {\n  const stat = await handle.stat();\n  if (!stat.isFile()) throw new Error(\\\"not a regular file\\\");\n  const size = stat.size;\n  const buffer = Buffer.alloc(size);\n  let offset = 0;\n  while (offset < size) {\n    const { bytesRead } = await handle.read(buffer, offset, size - offset, offset);\n    if (bytesRead === 0) return buffer.subarray(0, offset);\n    offset += bytesRead;\n  }\n  return buffer;\n} finally {\n  await handle.close();\n}\n```\n\nKey points:\n- `fs.promises.open()` returns a `FileHandle`; `stat()` and the read both operate on the same descriptor.\n- The read is bounded to the validated `stat.size`, so a concurrent writer cannot grow the file after validation.\n- The existing unlimited-input contract is preserved; no new per-file or aggregate caps are introduced.\n- `try/finally` guarantees `handle.close()` even when exceptions are thrown.\n\n## User Impact\n\n| Before | After |\n|--------|-------|\n| `stat(path)` \\u2192 TOCTOU race: file could be swapped/grown before read | fd pins the inode; read is bound to validated size |\n| Normal media input with valid files \\u2192 works | \\u2192 works (unchanged) |\n| File swapped/grown between stat and read \\u2192 could allocate beyond validated size | \\u2192 read is capped at the validated descriptor size |\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Capability CLI integration tests pass (109/109):**\n\n```\n\\u2713 |cli| src/cli/capability-cli.test.ts (109 tests)\n```\n\nThree integration tests specifically exercise the `image.edit` \\u2192 `readInputFiles` \\u2192 descriptor-bound read path (`openclaw infer image edit --file <path>`), writing temp PNG files and verifying `generationCall.inputImages[0].fileName` and `.mimeType` after the read pipeline:\n\n- `passes image output format, quality, and OpenAI hints through to edit runtime`\n- `forwards --count through to the image edit runtime`\n- `forwards size, aspect ratio, and resolution overrides for image edit`\n\nThe descriptor-bound pattern eliminates the TOCTOU race: `fs.promises.open()` returns a `FileHandle`, and both `stat()` and the read operate on the same descriptor, pinning the inode. Concurrent writers cannot grow the file between validation and consumption.\n\"\n",
